{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nOn Windows, `git show <rev>:<path>` run without `--` dies with exit 128 and `fatal: failed to stat '<rev>:<path>': Filename too long` when the working directory plus the argument exceeds MAX_PATH. Git stats each revision argument as a possible filename to rule out ambiguity, and it aborts on any stat error other than ENOENT. Measured in Windows `sweep (windows)` diagnostic run 44899637411 (2026-11-21 PST): `fsck_restore`'s `git show <sha>^:<ticket>/<event>.json` failed this way under a pytest temp dir. The same test passed under a shorter temp path (run 44899366277). With `git cat-file blob` (which takes only an object name) it passed (run 44900309390). cold-censorable-armedcrab fixed the `fsck_restore` sites (4f14a00093f, Gerrit 3511). This ticket covers the rest.\n\n## Sites on origin/main 39d78c81fd5 that read `<rev>:<path>` through `git show` with no `--`\nProduct (src/rebar), 12 reads:\n- src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py:98, :122, :164 (`tickets:.gitattributes`, `tickets:.gitignore`, `tickets:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_commands/init.py:440 (`tickets:.pre-commit-config.yaml`)\n- src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py:108 (`<rev>:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:151 (`<tickets ref>:<path>`)\n- src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:195 (`<spec>`, built as `<ref>:<prefix>rebar.toml` / `pyproject.toml`)\n- src/rebar/_store/compat.py:180, :274, :296 (`<remote ref>:<compat>`, `<commit>:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py:67 (`tickets:<projects.json>`)\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py:217 (`HEAD:<path>`)\n\nRepo scripts with the same shape, 4 reads: scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:517 (`<rev>:.github/complexity-baseline.json`, run by `make lint`), scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py:53, :56, scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py:43.\n\nSeveral product sites treat a non-zero exit as \"absent\", so a deep Windows path misreads an existing object as missing. Example: the `_init_ensures` units then re-create and commit a file that exists. Others (`bridge_fsck`, `_opcert_gate_config`, `check_complexity_baseline`) fail closed with an error on a store that is fine.\n\n## Root cause\nThe class is \"a revision-parsing git verb (`show`, `log`, `diff`, `rev-list`) given a `<rev>:<path>` argument with no `--`\". For those verbs git runs its filename-ambiguity check on every revision argument, which stats `<cwd>\\<rev>:<path>`. On Windows that stat fails with ENAMETOOLONG once the joined string reaches MAX_PATH, even though no file of that name exists or is needed, and git aborts. `git cat-file blob <rev>:<path>` resolves the object name only and never stats it (proven on the Windows runner by run 44900309390). `rev-parse <rev>:<path>` and `cat-file -e` resolve valid names without the stat too, so their existing uses are not in the class.\n\n## Approach\n1. Product and script reads: replace every `git show <rev>:<path>` above with `git cat-file blob <rev>:<path>` through the same wrapper, keeping each site's `check`, `text`, timeout and returncode handling unchanged. `cat-file blob` emits the same bytes as `git show` on a blob (no textconv runs in either), and exits non-zero for a missing path or ref just as `show` does, so every \"absent\" branch keeps its meaning. Update the `raw-git-ok` / docstring text that names `show` (`_opcert_gate_config._git`, `bridge_fsck._run_scan_git` and its scan docstring, the `operation=` label). No config key, env var or flag.\n2. Guard test so the class cannot come back: `tests/unit/test_rev_path_read_guard.py` AST-scans every `*.py` under `src/rebar` and `scripts`. For each call that is a git invocation (a callee name containing `git`, or an argv list literal starting with `\"git\"`), it finds the verb after git's own `-C`/`-c` options and reports:\n   - a `show`/`log`/`diff`/`rev-list` call with no `--` token that passes a `<rev>:<path>` argument: a string literal or f-string with a literal `:` that is not an option (`--format=...` is excluded), or a local name assigned one in the same function;\n   - a `show` call with no `--` and no commit-display flag (`-s`, `--no-patch`, `--stat`, `--name-only`, `--name-status`, `--format…`, `--pretty…`). That catches content reads whose argument arrives through a parameter (the `_opcert_gate_config` shape).\n   The failure message names file:line and the remedy (`git cat-file blob <rev>:<path>`, or end the revisions with `--`). The module also carries synthetic positive and negative cases that pin the detector (f-string, literal, local name, opaque parameter, `-s --format` metadata read, `cat-file blob`, `rev-parse <rev>:<path>`, trailing `--`, `argparse.add_parser(\"show\")`). Against origin/main the real-tree test fails listing the 16 sites; after the change it passes.\n3. Behaviour regression test: `tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py`. It builds a repo whose committed `tickets` branch holds every file the sites read, then adds a `--no-checkout` linked worktree (the shape of a real `.tickets-tracker`) whose path is padded so that `len(cwd) + 1 + len(argument) >= 260` while the worktree's own `.git` file stays well under MAX_PATH. One parametrized case per product read drives the real function against that worktree and asserts it found the committed object:\n   - `_gitattributes_unit`, `_gitignore_unit`, `_store_compat_unit`, `seed_projects_mapping_unit` return status `ok` (pre-fix on Windows: `changed` plus a commit);\n   - `init._commit_precommit` makes no commit;\n   - `reclaim_publish._record_at` returns the committed record;\n   - `bridge_fsck._unknown_event_types_from_ref` reports the committed unknown event type;\n   - `_opcert_gate_config._committed_toml` returns the committed table;\n   - `compat._remote_store_epoch`, `compat._remote_lineage_names`, `compat.remote_epoch_supersedes_local` read the committed record;\n   - `engine_comparison._fixture_files` returns the file content with 0 missing.\n   The test runs on every platform (on POSIX it is an ordinary functional test). On Windows it reproduces the MAX_PATH condition and fails before the fix. If the pytest temp dir is already too long to build the case, the test fails with that diagnostic instead of silently skipping.\n4. Existing test that stubs the old argv: `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py::test_scan_failures_raise_public_rebar_error` keys its fake on `args[0] == \"show\"`; change it to `cat-file`.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py\n- src/rebar/_commands/init.py\n- src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py\n- src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py\n- src/rebar/_store/compat.py\n- src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py\n- scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py\n- scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py\n- scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py\n- tests/unit/test_rev_path_read_guard.py (new)\n- tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py (new)\n- tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py\nNo `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/*.args` line belongs to this bug, so none changes.\n\n## Testing\n- Red/green: run the guard test against origin/main (fails, 16 sites) and on the fix (passes); record both in a comment.\n- Pre-merge Windows validation: push the exact fixed tree to `tmp/b5-comic-heavyset-jerboa`, dispatch `test.yml` there, and record the `sweep (windows)` run id plus evidence that `tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py` was collected and the job had 0 failures from it. To show the test bites, a second dispatch on `tmp/b5-comic-heavyset-jerboa-red` (the same tree with only the product and script changes reverted) must show the long-cwd cases failing on Windows. Delete both tmp branches afterwards.\n- AC evidence after merge: the first scheduled `test.yml` run on main whose head contains the merge commit; its `sweep (windows)` run id goes in a comment.\n- `make verify` through verify-slot.sh before the push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No `git show`/`log`/`diff`/`rev-list` call in `src/rebar` or `scripts` passes a `<rev>:<path>` argument without `--`; all 12 product reads and 4 script reads above go through `git cat-file blob`.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_rev_path_read_guard.py` fails on origin/main 39d78c81fd5 (listing the sites) and passes after the change (both outcomes recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py` fails on Windows without the product change and passes with it (pre-merge `sweep (windows)` run ids recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_rev_path_reads_long_cwd.py` passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the merge (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the pushed tree, and the change lands with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795379149985561001,"uuid":"6ea4e53d-0b4b-433d-ac76-339f59638a78"}